        "comments": "The assembly daMimPere1.hap1.1 is based on 67x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. HIC signal indicates this species is likely degenerated hexaploid (6n=90). The primary assembly contains one copy of each subgenome. The order and orientation of contigs along chromosome 2 is uncertain from 14.8 Mb to the end.",
